cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the lists and write-ups it produces, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "cosmos-search: a search of Gaia DR4 epoch photometry for slow fades and long dimming episodes"
abstract: >-
  Code and written results of a search of Gaia DR4 epoch photometry for stars that fade or brighten over
  years and for dimming episodes of weeks to years that neither the instrument nor known astrophysics
  explains, with secondary searches for short dips and for non-Keplerian astrometry. Thresholds are set
  from the release's own stars, recall is measured with injected signals, and candidates go through
  automated checks against independent surveys and a blind review with a measured false-positive rate.
authors:
  - given-names: Cora
    family-names: Shallit
repository-code: "https://github.com/corashallit/cosmos-search"
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 0.0.1
keywords:
  - Gaia DR4
  - epoch photometry
  - time-domain astronomy
  - variable stars
  - anomaly detection
  - technosignatures
